---
title: Totals
description: A small test recipe that measures most ingredients twice.
course: side
icons: [cheese, potato, egg]
---

Whisk the @flour{1%cup}, @sugar{1%tbsp}, @eggs{2}, @milk{120%ml}(1/2 cup) and @honey{1/4%cup} together.

Melt the @butter{12%oz} and stir in the @cheddar{4%oz}(1 cup, shredded).

Boil the @potatoes{500%g} until tender.

Fold in the @&flour{1/2%cup}, @&sugar{1%tsp}, @&eggs{1}, @&milk{240%ml}, @&honey{2%tbsp}, @&butter{8%oz}, @&cheddar{2%oz} and @&potatoes{1%kg}.

Top with the @parmesan{1/4%cup}(1 oz, grated) and @?parsley{2%tbsp}.

Serve with the @./good{}.
